-- **Trim by frame count, not seconds**: `-t <sec>` rounds up to the next
-  frame per segment (~+40 ms each) and the drift accumulates until later
-  cuts fall audibly off the beat. Convert bars to frames once
-  (1 bar @ 117.45 BPM / 24 fps ≈ 49 frames) and cut with
-  `-vf "select='gte(n,START)',setpts=PTS-STARTPTS" -frames:v N`.
+- **Quantize absolute cut boundaries, then subtract**. At constant frame
+  rate, compute `B[k] = floor((cut_time[k] - song_in) * fps + 0.5)` for each
+  planned cut (nearest frame, ties forward). Clip k needs `B[k+1] - B[k]`
+  frames. Use an exact rate such as `24000/1001`; do not repeatedly add one
+  rounded frames-per-bar value. At 117.45 BPM / 24 fps, 64 bars end at frame
+  3139; repeating 49 frames per bar ends at 3136. Use measured cut times
+  when the generated tempo drifts. Reject adjacent cuts that round to the
+  same frame, and keep the audio source in-point aligned with output zero.
+  Cut with `-vf "select='gte(n,START)',setpts=PTS-STARTPTS" -frames:v N`.
+  This bounds each cut's quantization error to half a frame; it does not
+  prove beat detection, source-clip adequacy or creative quality.
